cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "exploration: downstream exploratory analyses for Xenium / Proseg preprocessed data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "xenium-preprocess-pipeline contributors"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-01"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.PLACEHOLDER"                    # TODO after Zenodo mint
url: "https://example.org/xenium-preprocess"
repository-code: "https://example.org/xenium-preprocess"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - xenium
  - spatial-transcriptomics
  - exploration
  - region-annotation
  - tumor-distance
abstract: >-
  exploration is the downstream / optional analyses companion to the
  canonical xenium-preprocess output. It provides reusable primitives
  that augment a preprocessed AnnData without mutating it. First
  function: region-polygon + signed tumor-distance annotation (Tracy
  #31). Designed to be extended with additional exploratory analyses
  (QC, scoring, visualization, cross-sample comparisons,
  hypothesis-driven analyses) over time.
